  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-12-14T17:42:29.507Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The point of this is to allow world makers to create actual games within vrchat that would require something to be saved to the users account to make some form of basic way to remember progress. For example, say each world had the ability to make a single slot on the users account to store a number between 1 and 255, that way anytime the user leaves the world they can still rejoin or make a new instance and have the same amount of progress they had prior to leaving. This would make tycoon style games or adventure games with a shop possible and popular as any progress they made is perfectly maintained. and a step in the right direction towards having actual games within vrchat that aren't team deathmatch or flinging frisbees at each other even without access to proper scripting. and to my knowledge couldn't be exploited if the server only allowed numbers to be stored or accessed. (and would maybe only be stored if the player disconnects to avoid spamming the servers)\n\nI've personally been wanting to make an adventure style game however I know that it would have to be completed in one sitting as leaving would just reset the whole story of it or anything players acquired (of course a good way around that would be passwords but that would be needlessly complicated and difficult to make compered to just accessing a number assigned to a player ID and world ID and going from there.)",
